{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "51bc0b7d-ae00-8bd5-b520-b5aadcaf3df9",
  "created_at": "2026-01-07T14:52:35-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Luis Souza",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:47:38-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities, water and sewer billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:47:44-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hi. Luis Souza. I got a late fee on my water bill and I'm telling you, that check went out on time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:47:53-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I can look at that with you. What's the service address, Mr. Souza?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:47:59-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "458 Dixon Street. North End. Down from where the bank used to be, if you know it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:48:06-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, I know the area. Hang on one second while I pull it up. Dixon Street, 458. Okay, I see the account. And you're saying you mailed a payment?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:48:17-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I mailed it. Put it in the box myself, the one by the corner. I got the bill right here in my hand. Hold on. [pause] Hey, c'mere, give me your foot. Sorry, I got my grandson here, I'm tying his shoe with the phone on my shoulder."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:48:35-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:48:38-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So the bill says the date on it is December 12th. Due date, December 29th. I mailed that check the week before Christmas, easy, the 20th or so. So that's on time. And now there's a late charge on this new one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:48:54-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. So here's what I'm seeing. The bill is dated the 12th, due the 29th, like you said. Our system shows the payment posted on January 2nd. So it came in after the due date, which is why the late charge got added."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:49:10-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "January 2nd. That's two weeks! It's a stamp, a letter, it don't take two weeks to get across town."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:49:18-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, with the holidays the mail can get slow, and it can sit a few days before it's opened and entered. What matters on our end is usually when we receive it, not when it's mailed, though I can note on the account that you say it went out before the due date."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:49:38-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd appreciate that. I been paying this bill for years and never had a late fee. Not once."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:49:45-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I do see the history is clean. Let me put that note in. I can also send this over to the billing supervisor to review the late charge. They're the ones who can decide on removing it. I can't promise how it'll come out, but it'll get looked at."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:50:03-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fine. Do that. Because I'm not paying for the post office's problem."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:50:08-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. Do you still have the envelope or a check number, or the date it cleared on your bank statement?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:50:16-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I got the check stub. I don't have the envelope, who keeps the envelope? The stub says the 20th."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:50:24-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's helpful. I'll put the stub date in the note."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:50:29-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Now, another thing. Next time, I don't want to rely on the mail. Can I pay on a Saturday? Like, if I can't get down there during the week?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:50:41-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "City Hall's closed on Saturdays, but you've got options. You can pay online anytime, any day, with a card or a bank account. There's also a payment drop box outside City Hall that's available after hours, so you could drop a check in on a Saturday and it gets picked up the next business day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:51:01-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The drop box. Where's that, exactly? I'm not good with the computer."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:51:06-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's out front at City Hall on Broadway, near the main entrance. Just put the check in an envelope with your account number or the bottom of the bill, and it goes in the slot."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:51:19-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. And that counts as paid the day I put it in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:51:24-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Generally it's counted as of when it's collected, the next business day, so if you're close to the due date, give yourself a little cushion. If you drop it Saturday it'd be Monday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:51:37-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Monday. Okay. So the lesson is don't wait till the last minute, is that what you're saying?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:51:44-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A little bit, yeah. But in your case I get it, you were early. I've got the note on there and I'm sending it up for review."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:51:55-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "How long till I hear anything?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:51:58-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Usually a week or so. If you haven't heard anything by then, call back and mention you spoke with me. Is this a good number for you, the one you're calling from?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:52:10-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's 401-555-0166. That's the landline."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:52:13-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0166. I've got that on the note."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:52:17-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Hold on, he's going out the door with one shoe. Alright, thank you. Just get that fee off, will you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:52:25-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll get it to the right people, Mr. Souza. You take care, and have a good rest of your afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-07T14:52:33-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, you too. Bye."
    }
  ],
